# EVERY REMAINDER THIS MODEL CAN COMPUTE, BESIDE WHAT ITS FILING ESTABLISHED ABOUT THE SET IT
# SITS IN. One row per computable remainder: the extent its stack declared, what its coupling
# search reported, and any spillover somebody else observed into it.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ A REMAINDER IS ONLY MEANINGFUL IF THE LAYER SET IS CLOSED. `r = n - d` is a fact about
#    one layer, and the model then treats the stack as a set of independent quantizations. Two
#    things break that, and only one of them is about this document: nobody bounded the set, or
#    a pair it holds spills over. Nineteen of thirty-six remainders here sit in a set somebody
#    established; twelve sit in one nobody has asked about.
#
# ⛔⛔ THE VERDICT IS COMPUTED FOR EVERY REMAINDER, AND THAT IS THE ASSERTION RATHER THAN THE
#    ANSWER. `unbounded` is the honest state for a filing written to argue about three layers,
#    and it must never fail anything. What must fail is a remainder that reaches the arithmetic
#    without this question having been put to it at all.
#
# ⭐ `unbounded` IS NOT A SMALLER `scoped`. epistemics/scopes.sqlc has the argument: `scoped`
#   says somebody established what lies outside, `unbounded` says nobody looked. Folding them
#   would count a silence as a boundary.
-- layers/remainder.sqlc against pm:Stack/pm:scope, pm:couplings/pm:absent and entries/spillovers.sqlc.
SELECT r.filing, r.layer,
       sc.extent,
       cs.answer AS search,
       sp.observed_in AS spilled_from,
       CASE WHEN sp.observed_in IS NOT NULL THEN 'takes a spillover'
            WHEN sc.extent = 'unbounded'    THEN 'nobody bounded the set'
            WHEN cs.answer  = 'unmeasured'  THEN 'set bounded, pairs untested'
            ELSE 'bounded and the pairs answered' END AS standing
FROM      (
    :compose(layers/remainder.sqlc)
) r
LEFT JOIN (
    :compose(epistemics/scopes.sqlc)
) sc ON sc.filing = r.filing
LEFT JOIN (
    :compose(epistemics/coupling_searches.sqlc)
) cs ON cs.filing = r.filing
LEFT JOIN ( SELECT DISTINCT borne_by, from_layer, observed_in FROM (
    :compose(entries/spillovers.sqlc)
) x ) sp ON sp.borne_by = r.filing AND sp.from_layer = r.layer
